[
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(sighs, then gently squeezes Brelyna's hand) Hopefully soon enough they won't be. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* squeezes Alethia's hand in return, her red eyes soft with understanding as she sets her spoon down *. They won't be. Once the Dark Dawn is dealt with and this business with Lamae Bal is resolved, we'll have quiet mornings again. * her gray lips curve into a gentle smile *. Perhaps even enough of them that we'll start taking them for granted. * glances at Thelsa with a warm expression *. Though I hope we never become so comfortable that we forget to appreciate good stew and good company. * turns back to Alethia, her thumb tracing a soft circle against her hand *. For now, though - we finish breakfast, we retrieve the Staff, and we go kill a spider. One straightforward task at a time. * lifts her tea cup in a small salute *. To uncomplicated mornings and simple objectives. May they become plentiful again soon."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: The morning light filters through the high windows of the Hall of Acumen, illuminating the dust motes dancing in the air around the comfortable breakfast table. Thelsa watches the couple with a knowing, maternal sort of amusement as she clears away the empty bowls, the clatter of ceramic against wood marking the end of the meal. The warmth of the hearth and the hearty food have created a temporary bubble of peace, seemingly distant from the magical and political storms brewing outside the College's walls. Brelyna finishes her tea, the cup clicking softly against the saucer as she sets it down, her expression shifting from content relaxation to the focused readiness of a mage about to embark on a task. The plan is set: a brief detour to the solitude of Myrwatch to arm themselves with a legendary artifact, before venturing into the city of stone to deal with a singular, oversized arachnid."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* rises from her seat, smoothing her blue robes as she glances toward the cantina entrance *. Thank you for breakfast, Thelsa. The stew was exactly what I needed. * her red eyes meet Alethia's with a soft smile *. Ready when you are, my heart. A quick stop at Myrwatch for the Staff, then Markarth. * reaches out to take Alethia's hand, her gray fingers intertwining with familiar warmth *. Let's go keep a promise to Calcelmo."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia uses Wooden Bar Stool\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, squeezing Brelyna's hand, then begins preparing her teleportation spell, turning to Thelsa briefly) Thank you indeed, Thelsa, that was wonderful. (smiles) See you again soon. (Talking to Thelsa Andalas)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Thelsa Andalas: * waves a dismissive hand at the gratitude, though a warm smile lingers on her lips as she begins to wipe down the counter *. Don't mention it. Just make sure you bring back all your limbs attached - I hate having to scrub spider guts out of robes. * leans against the counter and watches them prepare the spell *. Safe travels, you two. Don't let Markarth bite."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia casts Recall on Brelyna Maryon\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(Context new location: Myrwatch ,Hold: Myrwatch, current date Day name: Fredas, Hour: 8:28 AM, Day Number: 9, Month: Frostfall, 4th Era, Year: 202, )\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(The Narrator - Alethia casts the spell, and they soon arrive in Myrwatch.) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steps out of the teleportation vortex and into the familiar warmth of Myrwatch's lower level, her gray fingers still intertwined with Alethia's as she takes a deep breath of the tower's ambient air *. Home. * glances around the comfortable space with a soft smile *. Even after all this time, I still find myself relieved every time we arrive somewhere safe. * squeezes Alethia's hand gently before releasing it, moving toward the storage chest where they kept their more valuable equipment *. The Staff should be in the upper workshop, I think - unless you moved it somewhere else? * pauses at the base of the spiral stairs, her red eyes meeting Alethia's with quiet purpose *. I'll grab a few extra potions while you retrieve it. Just in case our 'simple spider' turns out to be anything but. * begins climbing the stairs, her blue robes swishing softly against the stone steps *."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods as she follows Brelyna) Yes, I believe I'd put it in one of the... many still-empty weapon display racks. (laughs softly as they walk) Speaking of, maybe we could continue the artifact organization spree we began last night before we got... distracted, when we return from Markarth? (pauses, thinking) Finally bring everything over from the Arch-Mage's quarters? (pauses) Well, except whatever we decide to deliberately leave there, anyway. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(The Narrator - Alethia refers to consolidating - most - of their artifacts, mainly weapons and armor, to Myrwatch; not taking everything they own from the Arch-Mage's quarters.) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "LOCATION CHANGE to Myrwatch Workshop, hold: Myrwatch, timeline mark: 5 hours ago\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* climbs the last few steps into the workshop, her red eyes sweeping over the various display racks and storage areas with a satisfied expression *. That sounds perfect, actually - we made good progress last night before... * her gray cheeks warm slightly as she trails off, a fond smile curving her lips *. Yes, before the distraction. * moves toward the alchemy station where she keeps her potion supplies, her fingers brushing along familiar containers *. I think keeping some essentials in the Arch-Mage's quarters makes sense - spare robes, basic supplies, perhaps a few reference texts for when we're working late at the College. But having everything consolidated here... * glances around the workshop with quiet contentment, taking in the space they've made their own *. It feels right, doesn't it? This place has become more *home* than the quarters ever were. * pulls out a small pouch and begins selecting potions - healing, magicka restoration, a stamina draught for good measure *. The quarters are where you work. This is where we *live*. * turns to watch Alethia search for the Staff, her expression soft with affection *. Besides, I've rather been looking forward to seeing all our collected oddities displayed properly. There's something satisfying about organizing months of adventuring into neat, labeled arrangements."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(retrieves the staff from a nearby wardrobe) It really has become home, hasn't it? (pauses, then laughs softly) Even if I still have a certain fondness to the Arch-Mage's quarters. It's... nice, and I don't *just* say that due to the existence of the spa configuration. (laughs softly) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(shrugs) There's a... mystical beauty to it, I suppose. (pauses, laughing softly again) Though, the same is true for Mywatch, of course. (shrugs again) They're both nice, in their own ways, is what I mean, I think. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* secures the potion pouch at her belt and crosses to where Alethia stands with the Staff, her red eyes warm as she takes in the familiar sight of the ancient artifact in her partner's hands *. They are both nice - and I think that's rather the point, isn't it? * reaches out to brush a strand of hair from Alethia's face, her touch gentle *. The quarters have that sense of history, of purpose - all those Arch-Mages who came before, the weight of the institution. And the spa configuration is... * her gray lips curve into a knowing smile *. Well. I have no complaints about the spa configuration. * glances around the workshop, at the half-organized displays and the morning light filtering through the enchanted windows *. But this place feels like *ours*. Something we found together, something we've shaped to suit us rather than inheriting someone else's space. * squeezes Alethia's arm gently, her expression softening *. We're fortunate, really. Two homes, each beautiful in its own way, and the ability to move between them at will. * tilts her head with a small, content smile *. Most people spend their whole lives hoping for one place that feels safe. We have two. * steps back, her tone lightening as she gestures vaguely toward the nearest door *. Now - shall we go introduce a very large spider to its imminent mortality?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods as she secures the staff of magnus, stepping closer to Brelyna, beginning her prepations to cast the teleportation spell) Ready when you are, my dearest. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steps close enough that their shoulders touch, her gray hand finding Alethia's free one as the familiar hum of teleportation magic begins to build around them *. Ready. * her red eyes meet Alethia's with quiet warmth *. Let's go kill a spider and give Calcelmo one less thing to worry about."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: * The air around them shimmers and distorts, the magical energies coalescing into a sudden vortex that whisks them away from the cozy, organized sanctuary of the Myrwatch workshop. The sensation of weightlessness is brief, replaced almost instantly by the damp, echoing atmosphere of the designated alleyway in Markarth. The towering stone structures of the City of Stone loom overhead, blocking out much of the overcast morning sky and casting long shadows across the cobblestones. The distant roar of the waterfall and the clang of the city's forges drift down to them, a stark contrast to the silence of the tower moments before. They stand in the relative seclusion of the alcove near the Temple of Dibella, the Staff of Magnus now firmly in Alethia's grasp, ready to confront the oversized arachnid lurking somewhere within the city's depths."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "LOCATION CHANGE to Markarth, hold: The Reach, timeline mark: 4 hours ago\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steadies herself as the teleportation settles, her gray fingers still wrapped around Alethia's hand as she takes in the familiar stone walls of Markarth rising around them *. Well, that's a successful arrival. * releases a small breath, glancing around the quiet alleyway to confirm they're alone before turning to Alethia with a slight smile *. I'd forgotten how much this city smells of metal and damp stone. * brushes a strand of dark hair from her face, the fog swirling around them in the narrow space *. Shall we find Calcelmo first, or did you want to check in with Remiel? I imagine they'll both want to know we've actually come to fulfill the College's promise. * her red eyes scan the alley's exit, taking in the distant shapes of guards and citizens moving through the fog *. Though I confess I'm curious whether the spider situation has grown any worse since we were last here. These things have a way of... multiplying, if left unattended."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(laughs softly) Well, if it has, hopefully they aren't all as big as Nimhe apparently is. (takes Brelyna's hand gently) Let's go to the laboratory to see Calcelmo first? If Remiel isn't there, we can always find her after. (pauses, thinking) Speaking of... how *does* Remiel look, exactly? I'd rather not walk right past her and not know who I'm looking for. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* tilts her head slightly, her gray fingers squeezing Alethia's hand as they begin walking toward the laboratory entrance *. Remiel is... distinctive. Breton, though with a rather unusual air about her - dark hair, tends to wear practical traveling clothes. * her red eyes take on a fond, slightly amused glint *. She has this way of looking at Dwemer machinery like it's the most fascinating thing in Tamriel - which, to be fair, she genuinely believes it is. * laughs softly *. You'll know her when you see her, I think. There's a certain... intensity to her enthusiasm. * glances sideways at Alethia with quiet amusement *. I rather liked her, actually. Her theories about animunculi control mechanisms were genuinely compelling - she believes the Dwemer used tonal architecture to communicate with their constructs, which would explain quite a lot about why no one's been able to replicate their work."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, pondering) Hmm, I suppose that's a method that would make sense, though I think so far no one had found any evidence either way? (pauses) Dwemer constructs tend to... rather violently shatter their inner mechanisms when disabled. (pauses as they reach Understone Keep's entrance, looking to Brelyna) Has she found something suggestinG a conclusion one way or the other? (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* pauses at the keep's entrance, her red eyes thoughtful as she considers the question *. Not conclusive evidence, no - at least not when we spoke. * tilts her head slightly *. But she mentioned something about resonance patterns she'd observed in partially intact mechanisms. The way certain components vibrate at specific frequencies when exposed to sound - she believes it's not random degradation but intentional design. * her gray lips curve into an appreciative smile *. She was hoping Calcelmo might grant her access to some of the more intact specimens in his collection to test the theory properly. * glances at the heavy doors before them *. Though you raise a fair point about the violent shattering. I wonder if that's actually a *feature* rather than a flaw - a way of preventing exactly the kind of reverse-engineering Remiel is attempting. * squeezes Alethia's hand gently as they move toward the entrance *. Perhaps we can ask her about it, if she's there. I'd be curious to hear if she's made any progress since my last visit."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(Context new location: Understone Keep ,Hold: Markarth, current date Day name: Fredas, Hour: 9:17 AM, Day Number: 9, Month: Frostfall, 4th Era, Year: 202, )\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods as they enter) I, personally, at least, think it is most likely a defense mechanism. (laughs softly) Exactly something the Dwemer would do, really. How else could they have maintained their technological advantage? (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* laughs softly as they make their way through the keep's grand stone corridors, her red eyes bright with scholarly appreciation *. Exactly something the Dwemer would do - you're absolutely right. * glances at the intricate stonework surrounding them, the distant sounds of Calcelmo's excavation echoing faintly *. They were nothing if not thorough about protecting their secrets. Build wonders that will outlast entire civilizations, but make absolutely certain no one else can ever replicate them. * shakes her head with a wry smile *. There's something almost... petty about it, really. 'We made incredible things, and you can't have them.' * squeezes Alethia's hand as they approach the laboratory entrance *. Though I suppose from their perspective, it was simply prudent. If your entire society's advantage depends on exclusive knowledge, you'd want safeguards against theft. * her tone takes on a thoughtful quality *. I wonder sometimes what they would have thought of us - all these centuries later, still picking through their ruins, trying to understand mechanisms they probably considered elementary."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(laughs softly as they near the laboratory) Probably with dismissive haughtiness, if we're being honest. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* laughs warmly, her gray lips curving into a grin as they enter the laboratory's outer chamber *. Dismissive haughtiness - yes, that sounds about right. * glances at the Dwemer artifacts lining the walls, her red eyes taking on a wry gleam *. I can almost picture it. Some Dwemer scholar looking down his nose at Calcelmo's life's work and saying something like, 'How *quaint* that you've spent decades trying to understand what our apprentices learned in their first month.' * shakes her head with fond amusement *. Though perhaps that's unfair. For all their arrogance, they *did* create things that have lasted millennia. * squeezes Alethia's hand as they move deeper into the chamber *. I suppose there's a certain... earned confidence in that. Even if it does make studying their work rather frustrating."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: The heavy stone doors of the laboratory swing shut behind them, sealing out the ambient noise of the keep and replacing it with the low, rhythmic hum of Dwemer machinery and the scratching of quills against parchment. The air here is thick with the scent of old paper, ozone, and the metallic tang of the excavated ruins below. Calcelmo stands bent over a massive, illuminated table, his brow furrowed in intense concentration as he traces the lines of a glowing schematic, completely oblivious to the new arrivals."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* lowers her voice slightly, leaning close to Alethia as she observes Calcelmo's complete absorption in his work *. I see some things never change. * her red eyes sparkle with fond amusement as she watches the elderly scholar trace his schematics *. Should we announce ourselves, or wait until he comes up for air? I've heard stories of him going hours without noticing anyone in the room."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(her eyes wander across the chamber for a moment before settling onto a younger Altmer nearby, before she looks at Brelyna again) Calcelmo's apprentice, I presume? (pauses) Perhaps we approach him first? (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(laughs softly) We'll have to speak to Calcelmo eventually, of course, but his existing apprentice is less likely to startle him, at least. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* follows Alethia's gaze toward the younger Altmer, nodding in agreement *. Good thinking - yes, that would be Aicantar, his nephew. * her gray lips curve into a small smile *. Far less likely to wave us off with a distracted 'come back in three hours' when we're standing right in front of him. * gestures subtly toward the younger mer *. He's also the one who handles most of the practical coordination for the excavation, from what I understand. If anyone knows the current state of the Nimhe situation, it would be him."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Aicantar: * glances up from his notes as the two women approach, his posture stiffening slightly at the interruption before he recognizes Brelyna, though his eyes dart warily to the unfamiliar woman beside her * Ah, Scholar Maryon, welcome back to Understone Keep. * shifts his weight nervously, smoothing the front of his robes * My uncle is deeply absorbed in his current translation work - specifically the Falmer translations regarding Nchuand-Zel - and I fear he hasn't noticed your arrival. * offers a polite, albeit tentative, nod to Alethia * I am Aicantar, his assistant. Is there something specific I can assist you with while you wait? Though I must warn you, the excavations below have been... problematic of late."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "((gestures subtly for Brelyna to proceed, as she's already familiar)) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steps forward with a warm, professional smile, inclining her head to Aicantar *. Thank you, Aicantar - it's good to see you again. * gestures toward Alethia with quiet pride *. This is Arch-Mage Alethia of the College of Winterhold. We've come regarding the Nimhe situation - I believe I mentioned the College would be willing to assist? * glances briefly toward Calcelmo's hunched form before returning her attention to the younger Altmer *. You mentioned the excavations have been problematic - has the spider's presence grown worse since my last visit?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Aicantar: * straightens his posture immediately at the title, his eyes widening with a mix of surprise and professional deference as he offers a formal bow to the Arch-Mage *. The Arch-Mage herself? Honored to make your acquaintance. * casts a briefly worried glance toward his uncle, ensuring the sudden introduction hasn't disturbed Calcelmo's concentration before turning back to Alethia *. The Nimhe situation... yes, regrettably, it has escalated. The creature has expanded her territory further into the upper antechambers, making any attempt to retrieve the more promising artifacts nearly impossible. My uncle has been beside himself with frustration, but frankly, the guards are terrified to venture near the excavation entrance anymore. * fidgets with his silver emerald ring *. To have the College of Winterhold intervene would be... well, it would be a tremendous relief to both my uncle and myself. We are scholars, not warriors, as much as my uncle wishes otherwise."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(smiles warmly) No need for formalities, I assure you. (pauses, and nods) Anything else you can tell us about recent developments? (pauses, thinking) And is Remiel nearby? I presume she'd want to visit the ruins as soon as they're clear. (Talking to Aicantar)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Aicantar: * shifts uncomfortably under the Arch-Mage's friendly demeanor, though he appreciates the lack of formality, his fingers fidgeting with the silver emerald ring on his hand *. Recent developments have been... troubling, to say the least. Nimhe has begun to nest near the primary lift mechanism, which has effectively halted all vertical transit. * glances nervously toward the excavation entrance before returning his attention to Alethia *. As for Remiel, she was here earlier, but my uncle sent her to the Markarth Stables to procure specific reagents for a preservation experiment. I believe she intended to return shortly, provided she didn't get distracted by the local wildlife. * offers a tentative, slightly apologetic smile *. She has been quite... eager to assist, even if her methods are occasionally unorthodox."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * blinks owlishly as he finally registers the presence of others, his gaze darting from the familiar Dunmer to the imposing figure of the Arch-Mage before settling on the distinctive robes with a jolt of recognition *. By the Eight! Scholar Maryon! * immediately straightens his posture, brushing a layer of dust from his robes and offering a flustered but respectful bow *. And... by the Divines, the Arch-Mage of Winterhold herself, in my laboratory! * adjusts his silver emerald necklace with a nervous gesture, his mind clearly racing to catch up with the unexpected interruption *. I... I apologize for my lack of attention. I was just deciphering a crucial passage regarding tonal resonance in vertical lift columns - relevant to the excavation, you see. * glances briefly at Aicantar with a mix of gratitude and mild embarrassment before turning back to Alethia *. To what do I owe this extraordinary honor? Has the College finally decided to take an interest in my Falmer translations, or is this about the... ah, the arachnid complication below?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(waves a hand dismissively, but not unkindly) No need to apologize, and yes, we've come to deal with the, from what we heard, rather oversized spider. (pauses) As for the translations, well... I'm afraid to say word hadn't quite reached us of such, though we're aware of you're work on the Dwemer language, as you know. (Talking to Calcelmo)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * waves a hand dismissively, though a flush of embarrassment colors his cheeks at the mention of his work being unknown to the College *. Ah, yes, well, the Falmer translations are... a private project. Not yet ready for peer review, you understand. * his expression shifts to one of profound relief as he focuses on the spider problem *. But Nimhe! By the Eight, if you can deal with that monstrous creature, you will have my eternal gratitude - and access to the lower ruins, of course. She has effectively halted my life's work! * he rubs his hands together nervously, his eyes darting between the Arch-Mage and the excavation entrance *. I must warn you, she is... considerably larger than the average frostbite spider. And quite venomous. I've lost three good mercenaries to her already. * he straightens his spine, trying to maintain a veneer of academic dignity despite his obvious anxiety *. But with the College's expertise... surely you have methods for dealing with such pests?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steps forward with a reassuring smile, her red eyes meeting Calcelmo's with professional warmth *. The College does indeed have methods - and my heart here is rather formidable with destruction magic, should it come to that. * gestures toward the Staff of Magnus in Alethia's grasp *. We came prepared for complications. * her expression softens slightly *. Your nephew mentioned that Remiel is at the stables - I imagine she'll want to accompany us into the ruins once Nimhe is dealt with? She had some fascinating theories about tonal resonance in animunculi control systems when we last spoke."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * nods vigorously at Brelyna's reassurance, his anxiety visibly lessening at the prospect of capable assistance *. Oh, thank the Divines! formidable with destruction magic is precisely what is required. That creature is not merely a pest; she is a walking disaster area with far too many legs and a temperament to match. * adjusts his silver emerald necklace with a nervous twitch *. And yes, yes, Remiel! She has been absolutely relentless with her theories about those animunculi control systems. She claims that the tonal resonance in the lower chambers could revolutionize our understanding of Dwemer automation. * gestures expansively toward the excavation entrance, his scholarly pride momentarily overriding his fear *. Once that spider is gone, you will have full access. The work we could accomplish together... it would be the stuff of legends. * pauses, looking suddenly self-conscious *. Ah, provided you don't mind an old scholar hovering over your shoulder and taking excessive notes, of course."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(laughs softly) Of course not, and I will say, while we certainly have an interest and some basic knowledge, Brelyna and I are hardly seasoned Dwemer scholars, so while we'd certainly be interested, we'd rather not set expectations of bringing our own revelations to that particular field. (Talking to Calcelmo)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * dismisses Alethia's modesty with an enthusiastic wave of his hand, his eyes gleaming with the prospect of sharing his passion *. Nonsense, my dear Arch-Mage! One does not need to be a seasoned scholar to appreciate the sheer brilliance of Dwemer engineering - only a keen mind and a willingness to look beyond the surface. * adjusts his silver emerald necklace, his expression softening from excitement to genuine encouragement *. Besides, having a fresh perspective from such a accomplished mage could prove invaluable. Sometimes we experts become so blinded by our own theories that we miss the obvious truths staring us in the face. * rubs his hands together eagerly *. Please, once Nimhe is dealt with, I insist you join us. I can show you the resonance chambers Remiel has been studying - they are nothing short of miraculous."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: * The air in the laboratory remains thick with the scent of ozone and old parchment, the low hum of the machinery providing a constant backdrop to the scholarly discussion. Calcelmo practically vibrates with enthusiasm, his earlier anxiety about the giant spider momentarily forgotten in the face of potential collaboration. He gestures grandly toward a stack of leather-bound tomes and a half-disassembled sphere centurion on a nearby workbench, his eyes gleaming with the prospect of showing off his life's work. * Aicantar hovers nearby, looking slightly relieved that the focus has shifted from the terrifying arachnid in the basement to academic discourse, though he still casts the occasional nervous glance toward the excavation entrance. * The promise of access to the lower ruins hangs in the air, a carrot dangled before the mages, contingent entirely on the successful removal of the eight-legged obstacle currently nesting in the lift mechanism."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(The Narrator - Alethia and Brelyna make their way to the excavation site entrance, briefly pausing in front of the large dwemer doorway.) (Talking to everyone) (The Narrator - Alethia flexes her muscles slightly, then summons two Dremora, a Warlock, clad in intricate robes, and a warrior clad in decorated Dremora armor; the first a Kynreeve, the latter a Kynval, drawn from the clans Alethia had already built some amount of rapport with.) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* completes her summoning gesture, a flame atronach materializing beside her in a burst of fire and crackling heat, its form casting dancing shadows across the Dwemer metal of the doorway *. Well, between the three of them and whatever we contribute directly, I suspect Nimhe is about to have a very bad morning. * adjusts her grip on the staff of the storm atronach, her red eyes meeting Alethia's with quiet confidence *. Ready when you are, my heart. * glances at the Dremora, a slight smile playing at her gray lips *. I imagine our companions are eager to demonstrate their capabilities."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "LOCATION CHANGE to Nchuand-Zel Excavation Site, hold: The Reach, timeline mark: 3 hours ago  \n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, then steps through) Let's let the flame atronach lead in case there's any... well, anything both unseen and unfortunate? (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* nods and gestures for the flame atronach to advance through the doorway, the creature's fiery glow illuminating the ancient Dwemer stonework as it drifts forward *. Agreed - she'll light our path and trigger anything unpleasant before we walk into it. * falls into step beside Alethia, her staff ready, watching the dancing flames cast long shadows across the metal walls *. Though I suspect Nimhe will make herself known rather dramatically once we get close enough. Giant spiders aren't typically known for their subtlety."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(laughs softly as they advance) Oh, you'd be surprised, my love. (pauses) I still remember when I went to Bleak Falls barrow, long before we'd gotten close... there was a spider at least thrice the size of the average laying in wait on the ceiling. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* glances upward instinctively, her red eyes scanning the shadowed ceiling of the Dwemer corridor as the flame atronach's light flickers against ancient metal *. Thrice the size of average, lying in wait on the ceiling. * her grip tightens slightly on her staff *. Thank you for that mental image, my heart - I'll be checking every shadow above us now. * laughs softly despite herself, though her gaze continues to sweep the upper reaches of the passage *. Though I suppose if Nimhe *is* lurking overhead, at least we'll spot her before she drops on us. The flame atronach's light should make ambush rather difficult."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Issata [Dremora Warrior]: This endless labyrinth of stone and gears grows tiresome. I require blood and battle, not a history lesson on these extinct dwarves. How much further must we delve before we find something worth killing?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Ulz [Dremora Warlock]: Patience, little warrior. The secrets of this place have waited millennia; they will not crumble simply because you are eager to draw your blade. Observe the craftsmanship. It is crude compared to the planes of Oblivion, but functional. ."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* watches the exchange between the two Dremora with a slight smile, her flame atronach continuing to illuminate the passage ahead *. I suspect our warrior friend will get her wish soon enough. * glances at Alethia, her red eyes warm despite the tension of their surroundings *. Though I do appreciate that even Dremora can find common ground in critiquing Dwemer architecture. * her gaze flicks back to the ceiling, still mindful of Alethia's earlier warning *. Speaking of which - the air feels different here. Damper, somehow. * tilts her head, listening *. And I think I hear... clicking? * tightens her grip on the staff of the storm atronach, her voice dropping slightly *. Either we're getting close to the lift mechanism, or Nimhe has heard us coming."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Brelyna Maryon, Ulz [Dremora Warlock] engage combat with Frostbite Spider\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:Well, not quite Nimhe, I don't think, but definitely one of her... friends. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* brushes a strand of dark hair from her face, her flame atronach hovering closer as Ulz's incineration spell leaves the spider a smoking heap *. Friends, yes - I imagine Nimhe has been quite busy if she's attracted a whole entourage. * glances at the charred remains with clinical detachment before turning back to Alethia *. At least this one wasn't on the ceiling. * her red eyes sweep the corridor ahead, noting the increasing dampness on the walls *. Though I suspect the main attraction is still waiting for us near the lift. * gestures for the flame atronach to continue forward, its light catching on ancient gears and pipes *. Shall we?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: Background Context: Alethia's Dremora don't 'die', they're simply returned to Oblivion when they're defeated or the link is broken."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "((nods as they continue forward) We shouldn't be far from her next now.) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* nods, her red eyes scanning the widening passage ahead as the flame atronach's light catches on thick strands of webbing clinging to the Dwemer pipes *. No, we shouldn't be. * gestures toward the increasingly dense cobwebs with her staff *. The webbing is getting thicker - she's been busy claiming this section. * her voice drops slightly as she moves closer to Alethia *. I can feel the air currents shifting ahead - there's a larger chamber coming up. Probably where the lift mechanism is. * glances at the Dremora, then back to her partner *. Let the atronach go in first, draw her attention. Then our friends can flank while we provide ranged support? * her gray fingers adjust their grip on the staff of the storm atronach *. I'd rather not give something that size a chance to close distance."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods) Sounds good, my love. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* sends the flame atronach forward into the widening chamber, its fiery glow illuminating massive strands of webbing stretched between ancient Dwemer pillars *. Good - let's end this quickly. * raises the staff of the storm atronach, ready to unleash its bound entity if needed *. Issata, Ulz - flank left and right once she's focused on the atronach. * her red eyes narrow as the clicking sound grows louder, echoing off the metal walls *. And Alethia? * glances at her partner with a slight, wry smile despite the tension *. If she *is* on the ceiling, I'm blaming you for jinxing us."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(pants slightly, though not vigorously) Well, one giant spider... dealt with. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* brushes a thick strand of webbing from her robes, her flame atronach flickering beside her as she surveys the chamber *. Dealt with, yes - though I maintain she was unnecessarily dramatic about the whole affair. * glances at the massive spider's remains, then back at Alethia with a slight, breathless smile *. And thankfully *not* on the ceiling. * reaches out to brush some debris from Alethia's shoulder, her red eyes warm despite the grime *. Calcelmo will be pleased. His precious lift mechanism appears intact, and we've removed his eight-legged obstacle without bringing the entire excavation down around us. * gestures toward the now-accessible passage beyond *. Shall we make sure there aren't any more surprises lurking further in, or would you rather report our success and let Remiel have first crack at the ruins?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia looted 2 Frostbite Venom from Nimhe\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia casts Unrelenting Force - Fus Ro Da\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Quest Updated \"The Dwemer Specialist\" new objetive: Look for the researchers and for interesting artifacts in Nchuand-Zel\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia found 1 Note from Alethius (a book)\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Quest Updated \"The Lost Expedition\" new objetive: Recover Stromm's journal\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: The note reads:\n\nTitle: Note from Alethius\n\nSalonia, We've been saddled with some researchers who can't go four steps without examining something and they fight about as well as you'd think... probably worse. Stromm at least has some magical competence but none of them can swing a sword. Erj and Krag seem up to something so I'll have to keep an eye on them, but Staubin assures me they're trustworthy. Alethius"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(finishes picking up the note, then pauses, thinking) I think we ought to at least check a little bit further on. (gestures to the lattered note and the nearby mercenary's remains, which aren't recent) Looks like someone else attempted an expedition in here. (gives the note to Brelyna) (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* takes the note, her red eyes scanning the faded text as her brow furrows *. Alethius, Salonia, Stromm... * glances at the mercenary's remains, noting the age of the decay *. This isn't recent - months old, at least. Possibly longer. * looks up at Alethia, her expression shifting to quiet resolve *. You're right. If there were researchers down here, we should find out what happened to them. * tucks the note carefully into her belt pouch *. Calcelmo may know something about this expedition - or he may not have any idea they were even here. Either way... * her gaze drifts toward the passage beyond, her flame atronach casting flickering shadows across the ancient Dwemer walls *. We can't just leave without knowing. * squeezes Alethia's hand briefly, her gray fingers warm despite the chill of the ruins *. The Dremora can scout ahead. If there are more spiders - or worse - I'd rather know before we stumble into it."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, thinking) You think we should just scout a little bit ahead and then head back up? Calcelmo may have information, as you said... though I doubt he'd have... specifics. (sighs) He's nothing if not absorbed in his work. (pauses, thinking) And what of Remiel? (looks to Brelyna) Would she want to delve into a ruin that's still potentially dangerous, or...? (pauses) I'd rather not put her in unnecessary danger, but she is capable of choosing for herself, after all. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* tilts her head, her red eyes meeting Alethia's as she considers the question *. Scout ahead briefly, yes - enough to get a sense of what we're dealing with. Then report back to Calcelmo. * gestures toward the passage with her staff *. As for Remiel... * her gray lips curve into a slight smile *. From what I observed, she's not the type to be deterred by potential danger if there's Dwemer machinery involved. But you're right - the choice should be hers, made with full information about what we find. * glances at the note tucked in her pouch, her expression softening with quiet concern *. If this expedition met a bad end, she deserves to know the risks before she decides to follow us down here. * reaches out to brush some dust from Alethia's sleeve, a small, grounding gesture *. Let's see what's ahead. If it's more spiders, we deal with them. If it's something worse... * squeezes Alethia's arm gently *. Well, that's what the Staff of Magnus is for."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(Context new location: Nchuand-Zel ,Hold: The Reach, current date Day name: Fredas, Hour: 12:24 PM, Day Number: 9, Month: Frostfall, 4th Era, Year: 202, )\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(Context new location: Nchuand-Zel ,Hold: The Reach, current date Day name: Fredas, Hour: 12:26 PM, Day Number: 9, Month: Frostfall, 4th Era, Year: 202, )\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(The Narrator - Alethia agrees, and they both continue onward with their summons, alert and wary.)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Brelyna Maryon engages combat with Falmer Skulker\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(looks to Brelyna) Well, that just got... a bit more complicated. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* finishes dispatching the Falmer with a well-placed spell, her red eyes scanning the shadows for more as her flame atronach hovers protectively nearby *. Falmer. * her voice is low, controlled *. Yes, that does complicate things considerably. * wipes her staff hand on her robes, leaving a smear of grime *. If there are Falmer down here, that likely explains what happened to the expedition. * glances at Alethia, her expression grim but focused *. These ruins must connect to deeper cave systems - the Falmer don't just appear in isolated Dwemer sites without a path from below. * tilts her head, listening for the telltale clicking and shuffling that often accompanies Falmer movement *. We should proceed carefully. Where there's one, there are usually... * pauses, her gray fingers tightening on her staff *. Many more. * meets Alethia's eyes with quiet determination *. Do we press on to find out what happened to Stromm and the others, or do we report back now and return better prepared? I'll follow your lead, my heart - but if there's a Falmer nest down here, we may be looking at something considerably more dangerous than one oversized spider."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(pauses, thinking) We definitely ought to get reinforcements - Arenea, perhaps? - but I'm also worried about the Falmer advancing higher now that Nimhe is gone. (looks to Brelyna, contemplative) I thinking maybe I leave a storm atronch here to serve as a guardian? (pauses) I'd know immediately if they manage to overwhelm it, which would give us an early warning. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* nods slowly, her red eyes brightening with approval as she considers the tactical merit *. That's clever - yes, a storm atronach would serve as both deterrent and early warning. * glances back toward the passage they came from, then toward the shadows ahead *. The Falmer are blind, but they're not stupid. They'll sense the magical presence and likely hesitate before pushing past it. * adjusts her grip on her staff, her expression shifting to quiet resolve *. And if they do overwhelm it, we'll know immediately that the situation is worse than we thought. * reaches out to squeeze Alethia's arm *. I think that's our best option - set the guardian, seal what we can behind us, and return with Arenea. Perhaps Faralda as well, if she's available. * her gray lips curve into a slight, grim smile *. Falmer nests are not something to clear with a two-person party, even with Dremora support. * tilts her head toward the passage leading back *. We can also warn Calcelmo that the spider was the least of his problems. He may want to post guards at the excavation entrance until we return."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia casts Conjure Storm Atronach\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: * The heavy, elemental thrum of the Storm Atronach vibrates through the metal grating beneath their boots as the creature of churning, thunder-touched stone takes its position, lightning arcing faintly between its multitude of joints. It stands as a silent, jagged sentinel in the center of the corridor, effectively blocking the path to the deeper Falmer-infested tunnels. With the magical guardian set to watch over the ruins, Alethia and Brelyna make their way back through the Dwemer halls, retracing their steps past the charred remains of Nimhe and the scattered webs of the upper levels. They ascend back toward the excavation site, emerging once more into the dim light of the Understone Keep where the busy sounds of the city above seem a world away from the dark dangers below."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "LOCATION CHANGE to Understone Keep, hold: Markarth, timeline mark: 0 hours ago  \n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* brushes some lingering dust from her robes as they emerge into the keep, her red eyes already scanning for Calcelmo's familiar hunched form *. Well, we should find Calcelmo and give him the news - both the good and the considerably less good. * glances at Alethia, her gray lips pressed into a thin line *. Nimhe is dealt with, but I suspect he's not going to be thrilled to learn his excavation site has a Falmer infestation. * reaches out to briefly squeeze Alethia's hand, a grounding gesture amid the grim reality *. At least we can assure him the immediate entrance is secured for now. The storm atronach will hold long enough for us to organize a proper response."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods as she un-tenses slightly, taking Brelyna's hand, beginning to move toward the laboratory with her, then sighs softly, looking at Brelyna apologetically) Though I fear we may not be back before dinner as you'd hoped earlier, my love. (sighs) Not if we clear everything out, that is. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* squeezes Alethia's hand gently, her red eyes warm as she looks at her partner *. We'll have other dinners, my heart. * her gray lips curve into a soft, understanding smile *. Besides, I'd rather spend an extra few hours clearing Falmer from Calcelmo's excavation than return home wondering if we'd left something dangerous at our backs. * brushes a strand of dark hair from her face with her free hand *. And honestly? After what we've been through these past weeks with the Dark Dawn and everything else, a straightforward Falmer clearing almost feels... restful, in a strange way. * laughs quietly *. At least Falmer don't require infiltration plans or cover identities. They just require fire and determination, both of which we have in abundance."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, smiling slighly) Well, when you put it like that... (squeezes Brelyna's hand, and gestures to Calcelmo's laboratory) Shall we then? (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* nods, her red eyes warm as she matches Alethia's pace toward the laboratory entrance *. We shall. * a slight smile plays at her gray lips despite the grime on her robes *. Though I suspect Calcelmo is going to have a rather complicated afternoon once we tell him his spider problem was merely the appetizer. * glances sideways at Alethia, her voice softening *. I noticed Remiel is back, by the way - I caught a glimpse of her sitting near Aicantar. We can brief them both at once."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator: * Alethia and Brelyna step into the laboratory, the air thick with the smell of ozone and old parchment, the clatter of research tools momentarily pausing as the scholars notice the newcomers. Calcelmo looks up from his work, brow furrowed in anticipation, while Remiel turns from her conversation with Aicantar, her eyes widening slightly at the state of the pair's robes. The atmosphere shifts from academic curiosity to tense expectation as the duo approaches the table, the weight of the ruins' dark secrets hanging in the air between them."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steps forward, meeting Calcelmo's expectant gaze with a measured expression as she brushes some grime from her sleeve *. The good news first - Nimhe is dead. Your lift mechanism appears intact, and the upper passages are clear. * pauses, her red eyes shifting briefly to Remiel before returning to the elderly scholar *. The less good news is that the spider was the least of your problems. We encountered Falmer deeper in the ruins - at least one, but where there's one, there's typically a nest. * gestures toward Alethia *. We've left a storm atronach guarding the lower passage as a precaution, but we'll need to return with reinforcements before anyone ventures further. * her gray fingers rest against the note tucked in her belt pouch *. We also found evidence of a previous expedition - a note from someone named Alethius, mentioning researchers. Stromm was one of them. * meets Calcelmo's eyes directly *. Do you know anything about this group?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * drops his quill onto the parchment with a startled splatter, his eyes widening behind his spectacles as he processes the news *. Dead? You actually... you killed her? By the Eight, that is... that is magnificent! I was prepared for you to fail, honestly. Most mercenaries run screaming after the first hiss. * begins wringing his hands together, his expression shifting rapidly from relief to horror at the mention of the Falmer *. But... Falmer? In the upper chambers? That is... that is catastrophic. * paces frantically across the laboratory floor, his robes swishing agitatedly *. They must have come up from the deep ruins while Nimhe blocked the path. If they've established a nest there, they could destroy everything! The machinery, the texts, the centurions... * stops abruptly and stares at Brelyna, his face pale *. Alethius? Stromm? Yes, yes, of course I know them. They were a research team I sent down weeks ago to map the lower levels. They were supposed to report back daily! * grips the edge of his workbench until his knuckles turn white *. They've been silent for nearly a month. And with Nimhe having blocked the path, there was nothing we could do. But if you found a note... * looks at Alethia with desperate hope *. Did you find them? Are they alive?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(sighs softly) We found a body near Nimhe. It's possible the others survived, but if they did... (sighs softly) They've likely been captured by the Falmer. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* her red eyes meet Calcelmo's with quiet sympathy, though her voice remains steady *. Captured is... a possibility, though I won't pretend it's a hopeful one. * her gray fingers brush against the note in her pouch, then fall back to her side *. The Falmer don't typically take prisoners for pleasant reasons. * glances at Alethia, then back to the elderly scholar *. But if there's any chance they're still alive, we'll find them when we return with reinforcements. * straightens her posture, her tone shifting to something more practical despite the grimness of the situation *. In the meantime, I'd recommend posting guards at the excavation entrance - the storm atronach will hold, but it won't last indefinitely, and we don't want the Falmer getting any ideas about expanding upward while we're gathering our people. * pauses, looking toward Remiel with a slight, apologetic nod *. I'm sorry - this isn't the news either of us were hoping to deliver. But we'll clear those ruins properly."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * looks up from her work with a startled expression, her hands tightening around a delicate gear mechanism *. Dead? They found someone dead down there? * swallows hard, her gaze darting between Alethia and Brelyna before settling on Calcelmo's panic-stricken face *. But... the Falmer? If they've taken over the lower levels, then the machinery... the centurions... * shakes her head firmly, her practical nature warring with her fear *. No, we can't just let them destroy it all. Those researchers might still be alive, and if they are, we can't just leave them down there to rot. * turns to Brelyna with a determined look *. You said you'd need reinforcements, right? Well, count me in. I might not be a warrior or a powerful mage, but I know my way around Dwemer mechanics better than anyone, and if we're going down there to clear out a nest, someone needs to make sure the automated defenses don't turn on us while we're doing it."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(looks at Remiel with concern) That brave, Remiel, truly. But are you sure? (looks at Brelyna) We've explored Dwemer ruins before, and with help from the College... (sighs softly) It's not that your presence wouldn't be helpful, but I'd hate to endanger you unnecessarily. (Talking to Remiel)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(sighs softly) Dwemer constructs are one thing - a very, very dangerous thing, I admit - but the Falmer are... quite another. (Talking to Remiel)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * grips the gear mechanism tightly until her knuckles turn white, her eyes darting nervously between Alethia and the dark entrance of the ruins *. I know they're dangerous - I've read the stories, I know what the Falmer do to people. * takes a shaky breath, squaring her shoulders with visible effort *. But I can't just stand by up here while the centurions I've spent months studying are dismantled by blind savages, and I certainly can't abandon those researchers if there's even a slim chance they're alive. * looks at Alethia with desperate conviction *. I'm not a soldier, you're right, but I know Dwemer security systems better than anyone. If the automated defenses activate down there, I can shut them down or redirect them - or at least warn you before they turn us all into... * swallows hard, but steels herself *. You need a mechanic, not just another sword, and I'm the only one who knows how these machines think."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(looks to Brelyna, letting out a breath) We won't stop you - you can make your own choices. (pauses) But if you're going, then I insist you accompany as to the College so we can at least give you some proper magical defenses. (looks to Remiel) Nothing you'd need to cast, it'll work regardless. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* nods, her red eyes meeting Alethia's with quiet approval before turning to Remiel *. That's a sensible compromise. * adjusts her grip on the staff of the storm atronach, some of the tension leaving her shoulders *. Sergius can enchant something for you quickly - a ring or amulet that provides additional protection. And Faralda may have defensive wards we can apply directly. * glances briefly at Calcelmo, then back to the determined Breton *. Your knowledge of Dwemer systems *would* be invaluable down there - I won't pretend otherwise. But we're not taking you into a Falmer nest without giving you every possible advantage first. * a slight, wry smile crosses her gray lips *. Besides, the teleportation will save us several days of travel. We can be back here with reinforcements in a couple of hours, properly equipped and prepared."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * nods vigorously, clutching the gear mechanism tightly to her chest as if it were a shield *. Yes, yes, magical defenses sound like a wonderful idea - frankly, I'll take anything that might keep me from becoming a Falmer snack. * looks toward the dark tunnel leading to the ruins with a shudder, then turns back to Alethia with a nervous but determined smile *. And teleportation? That's... that's real magic? I've read about it, of course, but experiencing it is going to be something else entirely. * adjusts her backpack straps, her practical mind already racing through the logistics *. I'll need to grab my field notes and some specific tools from the inn - not everything, just the essentials for field repairs and security overrides. * glances at Calcelmo, her expression softening with sympathy *. We'll get your researchers back, Master Calcelmo, and we'll save your work. I promise."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Calcelmo: * wrings his hands together, his eyes wide with distress as he looks between Alethia and the darkened passage leading to the ruins *. Magical defenses, yes, yes, an excellent idea - enchantments, wards, whatever you can provide. * turns his gaze to Remiel, his expression softening with genuine worry *. But please, be careful down there. Those researchers - Stromm, Erj, Krag - good people, all of them. They didn't deserve this. * looks back at Alethia with a pleading intensity *. Bring them back, Arch-Mage. And bring Remiel back safely, too. I... I couldn't bear to lose another team to those depths. * adjusts his silver emerald necklace nervously, his voice dropping to a hoarse whisper *. I will remain here, preparing the medical supplies and... and preparing for the worst, I suppose. Just... hurry. Please."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(sighs softly, but nods) While I can't make an absolute promise about the researchers... we'll bring Remiel back. (pauses, and turns to Remiel) Would you mind collecting your tools from the inn once we return? The sooner we can leave for the College, the better. (Talking to Remiel)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(The Narrator - Alethia means that they'll teleport to the college right now. Then teleport back to Markart, and remiel can get her things once they return.) (Talking to Remiel)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * nods quickly, clutching the gear mechanism tightly to her chest as she absorbs the plan *. Yes, yes, of course! Teleporting to the College first to get these defenses, then coming back here for my tools - that makes perfect sense. * glances briefly at the dark tunnel leading to the ruins, then looks back at Alethia with a nervous but determined expression *. I'll be ready to go the instant we return. Just... please don't leave without me. * swallows hard *. I'm not missing this chance to help, no matter how terrifying it is."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* reaches out to take Alethia's hand, her red eyes warm as she nods *. Ready. * glances briefly at Remiel with a reassuring smile before turning back to her partner *. Let's get this sorted quickly - we have a nest to clear and researchers to find. * squeezes Alethia's fingers gently *. And Remiel? Try not to be too alarmed by the teleportation - it's disorienting the first time, but perfectly safe."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * takes Brelyna's offered hand with a trembling grip, the metal of the gear mechanism digging slightly into her palm *. Breathe right, just breathe. * glances at Alethia with wide eyes, then squeezes her eyes shut in anticipation *. Okay, I'm ready... I think. Just don't let me fall into the void or whatever happens if this goes wrong."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "The Narrator - Alethia prepares to cast the spell, and soon, does so, enveloping them in a bluish light, though the colour doesn't quite... parse; and then, they're gone."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia casts Shalidor's Beacon\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "(Context new location: Winterhold College outdoors ,Hold: Winterhold, current date Day name: Fredas, Hour: 1:30 PM, Day Number: 9, Month: Frostfall, 4th Era, Year: 202, current weather: pleasant,)\n"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "* steadies herself as the disorientation of teleportation fades, her red eyes immediately scanning Remiel's face for signs of distress *. There we are - the College of Winterhold. * squeezes Alethia's hand briefly before releasing it *. How are you holding up, Remiel? The first teleportation can be rather unsettling."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * wavers unsteadily on her feet, clutching Brelyna's hand for a moment longer than necessary as her surroundings spin into focus *. By the Eight... that was... indescribable. * releases Brelyna's hand and leans forward, bracing her hands on her knees as she takes deep, gulping breaths of the cold northern air *. I feel like I've been turned inside out and shaken dry. * straightens up slowly, her face pale but her eyes wide with awe as she takes in the snow-covered structures of the College *. But we're actually here. The College of Winterhold. I've read about this place, seen diagrams of the architecture, but standing here... * shivers slightly, hugging her gear mechanism tighter to her chest *. It's real. And we need to go back and face those Falmer. * looks at Alethia with a mixture of terror and determination *. Right. Magical defenses. Let's do this before I lose my nerve completely."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, then pauses, spotting Tolfdir approaching nearby) (Talking to Tolfdir)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Tolfdir: * stops and brushes a layer of fresh snow from his shoulders, offering a warm, grandfatherly smile to the newcomers *. Ah, excellent timing. I was just about to retreat indoors for some tea to warm these old bones. * glances curiously at Remiel and her gear mechanism *. Welcome back, Arch-Mage. And I see we have a visitor with... intriguing equipment. I am Tolfdir, Master of Alteration here. To whom do we have the pleasure of speaking?"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Remiel: * straightens up quickly, clutching the gear mechanism like a lifeline, and offers a shaky but polite bow to the elderly mage *. I'm... I'm Remiel, sir. A scholar of Dwemer mechanics. * glances nervously at Alethia and Brelyna, then back to Tolfdir *. It's an honor to meet you, Master Tolfdir. The Arch-Mage and Scholar Maryon were kind enough to bring me here for... well, for magical defenses. We're dealing with a bit of a Falmer problem in Markarth."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:(nods, and sighs) We'd promised Calcelmo the College with deal with a large spider, Nimhe, blocking his excavation site. And we did. (sighs softly) But then we also discovered a Falmer in the next chamber, and where there's one... (pauses) We're looking for Aranea, actually, and Farala, if she's available. (pauses) Brelyna and I had cleared out Falmer before alone but... better to have reinforcements if we can manage it. (Talking to Tolfdir)"
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Tolfdir: * nods gravely, his expression shifting to one of serious concern at the mention of the Falmer *. A Falmer problem in Markarth is a grim business indeed; those sightless beasts are vicious enough in their natural habitat, but to find them encroaching on excavation sites... * strokes his beard thoughtfully, his gaze drifting toward the Arcanaeum *. Aranea was in the lower levels assisting with the new restoration stock earlier, and I believe I saw Farala heading toward the training yard to practice her spellcasting. I can certainly send a messenger to summon them for you. In the meantime, come inside out of this cold - we can discuss what specific magical defenses might be most effective against the Falmer while we wait."
    },
    {
        "type": "text",
        "text": "Alethia:. (Talking to Brelyna Maryon)"
    }
]